boats_project11/issues/138) FCU reconfig + tide/chart-datum chain** — bench-validated; needs on-water confirmation. **Prerequisite for sonar/survey data quality** at the lake. Highest priority.\n2. **One CLEAN survey run** (no buoy firefight) — the run #173/#186/#201 never delivered. Validate on sustained clean lines:\n   - **Turning behavior — velocity_smoother now LIVE** (seafloor #36, PR #37 merged 2026-06-02). 240 yaw is now **accel-governed** (`max_accel` yaw ±0.5 rad/s², ~2 s ramp to the full 1.0 rad/s speed cap), the fix for the #197 yaw-step snap-roll (±30°). Check, in priority order:\n     - **Snap-roll gone** — joining a line from near-stop should no longer induce the ±30° roll. If it still rolls, *lower* the yaw accel; if turns feel sluggish on line transitions, *raise* it (tuning table in the seafloor #36 plan).\n     - **`scale_velocities: true` surge coupling** *(open decision)* — watch whether surge drops on the straightaway during aggressive turn-rate changes (the smoother scales surge down to preserve heading vector). If it costs survey speed, flip to `scale_velocities: false` (independent per-axis clamping).\n     - **Autonomy-stop latency** — the smoother adds a ~1 s `velocity_timeout` hold + decel ramp on cmd_vel after the controller goes silent. Confirm autonomy-stop (end-of-mission, hover engage, Goto/override) still yields a *prompt* stop. Independent of the RC / Standby→MANUAL handoff path.\n     - **Reflex Collision Monitor still gates** — the smoother now sits UPSTREAM of the reflex monitor; confirm the binary slowdown/stop still fires correctly on the smoothed input (reflex safety floor must be unaffected).\n   - **Planner turn radius** (#124 §2: planner min radius 1.5 m) — still the deliberative-side limit; confirm clean-line geometry.\n   - **Cross-track / line-following** (#164) — #201 clean stretches held |XTE| median 0.47 m; confirm on a sustained clean line.\n   - **Hover stop-point (#33)** at *survey speed* — #201 only saw low-speed hovers (engagement overshoot not separable from current wander).\n3. **Mid-line resume (#58)** — re-test if the resume-from-nearest-ahead fix lands; otherwise confirm the documented workaround behaves (hover-hold / clear+resend).\n4. **Mission re-send (#35)** — confirm which path is active (same-type-latch fix vs replace-task).\n5. **OTH validation ([#130](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130))** — Starlink-only + a *completed* survey (lake is OTH-routine).\n6. **Autonomous obstacle avoidance** — the costmap-delivery fix landed (nav #56 / PR #61); the avoider-ahead-replan (nav #57) has **not**. So avoidance is still **not** class-ready — operate on the **fallback** (watch + exclusion zones + manual override).\n\n## Pre-flight / setup checks\n\n- **velocity_smoother is now in the stack by default** (seafloor #36 merged 2026-06-02) — no manual re-enable needed. See the turning-behavior checks above for what to validate (snap-roll, scale_velocities, stop-latency, reflex gating). NOTE: gitcloud/field hosts get it only after the seafloor jazzy→gitcloud resync.\n- **Costmap-over-bridge:** the nav #56 QoS fix **landed (PR #61, merged 2026-06-02)** — **validate on-water that the windowed costmap delivers to CAMP WITHOUT the manual `rqt_udp_bridge` subscriber** (the fix carries a \"confirm via controlled reproduction\" caveat). If it regresses, the `rqt_udp_bridge` hack remains the documented fallback. NOTE: gitcloud/field hosts only get the #56 fix once nav PR #55 also merges and gitcloud is resynced.\n- **SV / sound_speed** dropouts — watch (#163); `sound_speed_bridge` warned heavily on #201.\n- git-bug → gitcloud propagation done so field hosts see this issue.\n\n## Operator readiness (boat-free, before the class)\n\n- Operator perception display ([unh_marine_autonomy#127](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_autonomy/issues/127)).\n- Student deployment guide (#18).\n- Fallback SOP drilled: manual override / RC takeover + exclusion zones.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Date TBD** — set the title date at activation (`/start-deployment`).\n- Prior deployment: #201 (PR #204). Roadmap `docs/roadmap.md` is the durable carry-over.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1780413256,"nonce":"6Ro5XrbeQOufKlsHFGjVbya9H5M=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABEIINJ87Ap7Cw"},"target":"de8cdaddaa1049294aaa43c62e2816cfac4b01b72aef68916bd39abe86b2bc9f","message":"## Purpose\n\n**Pre-class shakedown at the UNH pier** (Judd Gregg / Chase Ocean Engineering —\nsaltwater, tidal, crane launch; NOAA Fort Point tides). Three goals:\n\n1. Confirm the boat can still **run survey lines** (under control, end to end).\n2. Confirm the **sonar + associated sensors work and are ready for students to\n   integrate software-wise**.\n3. **Re-test OTH.**\n\nThis is **not** the Lake Massabesic survey — it de-risks it. Pre-staged so\n`/start-deployment` activates it. Carry-over from #201 (PR #204) + `docs/roadmap.md`.\n\n\u003e **Out of scope:** autonomous obstacle avoidance. Not class-ready (costmap-delivery\n\u003e fix #56 unvalidated on-water, avoider-ahead-replan #57 open). Operate on the\n\u003e fallback (watch + exclusion zones + manual override); don't burn the run on it.\n\n## Goal 1 — Survey-line capability\n\n- **A clean survey run** — #173/#186/#201 were all buoy/perception days; this never got delivered.\n- **velocity_smoother re-enabled (seafloor #36, CLOSED 2026-06-02)** — the accel/yaw limiter is back in the cmd_vel path (controller→`cmd_vel_nav`→**smoother**→`cmd_vel_smoothed`→Collision Monitor). **First validate the boat still controls smoothly with the smoother back in**, then:\n  - **Turning limits (#124 §2)** — now unblocked; check helm yaw cap 1.0 rad/s + planner min radius 1.5 m on apron turns.\n- **Cross-track / line-following (#164)** — sustained clean lines (#201 clean stretches held |XTE| median 0.47 m).\n- **Mid-line resume (#58)** + **m