** — sensor streams available + documented enough for students to start integrating software against.\n\n## Goal 3 — OTH re-test ([#130](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130))\n\n- Starlink-only + a *completed* survey line at range; keep an eye on the topic-budget / saturation envelope.\n\n## Pre-flight / validate landed config changes\n\nSince the last clean validation the deployed config drifted — confirm each behaves:\n- **velocity_smoother re-enabled** (#36) — see Goal 1.\n- **Costmap-over-bridge (#56 fix, PR #61, merged 2026-06-02)** — validate the windowed costmap reaches CAMP **without** the manual `rqt_udp_bridge` subscriber (fix carries a \"confirm via controlled reproduction\" caveat); the hack is the documented fallback if it regresses. NOTE: field hosts get #56 only after nav PR #55 merges and gitcloud is resynced.\n- **`sea_surface_layer` tunes** (#201 current-best, unvalidated) + **CollisionSlowdown reverted to the tested 20 m / 0.3** — confirm behavior; sea_surface tuning remains a replay-tuner job (perception #26).\n- **Segmentation timestamp fix** ([unh_marine_perception#28](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/28), PR #29) — segmentation `Image` is now stamped from the OAK device capture time, not `now()` (was a constant ~123.5 ms late → stale camera pose → close buoys walked across costmap cells and never marked). Two-tier verify:\n  - **Stamp correctness (bench/dock, no water needed):** with the OAK powered and the fixed build running, record a fresh `*_ffmpeg_seg` slice and confirm **`seg_stamp − ff_stamp ≈ 0`** per frame (was a tight 123.5 ms). Same source frame + device clock ⇒ equality is the definitive proof. *This is the cheap gate — do it before relying on the fix.*\n  - **On-water:** the port horizon overlay sits on the true horizon through the pier-departure turn and a close buoy marks in the regenerated costmap; `sea_surface_tuner` δ-sweep best-aligns at δ≈0 (was −123 ms). NB the existing 05-29 