ed with the on-water checks it now needs.\n\n**What to check on the water with the smoother live** (detail in the body, item 2):\n- **Snap-roll gone** — the #197 ±30° roll on near-stop line-joins should be eliminated by the yaw accel cap (±0.5 rad/s²); tune up/down per the #36 plan table if sluggish/still rolling.\n- **`scale_velocities: true` surge coupling** *(open decision)* — if aggressive turns visibly slow the straightaway, flip to `scale_velocities: false`.\n- **Autonomy-stop latency** — the added ~1 s `velocity_timeout` + decel ramp must still yield a prompt autonomy stop (separate from RC/Standby handoff).\n- **Reflex Collision Monitor** — smoother is now upstream of it; confirm the binary stop/slowdown still gates on the smoothed input.\n\nReview (Claude + Copilot adversarial, 0 must-fix) verified the wiring against the installed Nav2 binaries; these four are behavioral checks that only the water can settle.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1780413256,"nonce":"m+/wyzG2qJn4g6hNz4uJ2yZiWEQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABEIINJ88AAAAGHEOiJw"},"title":"Deployment TBD: UNH pier shakedown — survey lines + sensor/sonar readiness + OTH (pre-class)","was":"Deployment 2026-06-02: UNH pier shakedown — survey lines + sensor/sonar readiness + OTH (pre-class)"},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780416805,"nonce":"qhVNu2otqmNN6OeP9S8t+W8Cf74=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEnD30Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/205#issuecomment-4604360657"},"message":"## Sea-surface costmap / buoy-marking — what to tweak once the timestamp fix is in\n\nContext (2026-06-02 investigation of the close-buoy-not-marking class, #186): root\ncause is the segmentation output stamped at *publish* time instead of\n*frame-capture* time — a constant **~123 ms stale pose**. Fix in progress:\n**rolker/unh_marine_perception#28**. Until that's built onto the boat, **no live\nparameter compensates** — params only change how aggressively a wrongly-posed\nobservation marks, trading a missed buoy for phantom/displaced obstacles.\n\n### This run, BEFORE #28 is on the boat — characterization only\n- Leave the sea-surface costmap params at defaults. Do **not** tune against the\n  stale pose (that's how the max-pool/backstop aggressiveness got over-fit).\n- Confirm the symptom live: horizon overlay / costmap mark sits right going\n  straight \u0026 slow, drifts off mid-turn (error ∝ turn rate).\n\n### AFTER #28 is built + verified — tune live, no rebuild\nVerify the fix first: fresh bench bag → `seg_stamp − ff_stamp` ≈ 0 (not 123 ms);\nor live horizon tracks through a turn.\n\n1. `max_pool_bins=false` first — with a stable pose the buoy should mark by normal\n   accumulation; max-pool suppresses clearing near contacts and was likely\n   compensating for the smear.\n   `ros2 param set /bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap sea_surface_layer.max_pool_bins false`\n   *(confirm node/plugin name on the boat)*\n2. Open-water false-positive check (no real obstacles) — watch for spurious lethal\n   cells from the graded gate (`obstacle_prob_min`) + backstop.\n3. Other live knobs if needed: `lethal_threshold`, `obstacle_clamp`, `clear_floor`,\n   `free_threshold`, `decay_half_life_s`, `max_range`, `min_grazing_angle_deg`.\n\n**Order matters: code fix first, then param re-tuning.** Tuning before the fix\nmis-trains the params.\n\nRefs: rolker/unh_marine_perception#28 (root cause + evidence), projection-review\nnotes (2026-06-02 session), rolker/marine_perception_tools#2 (tuner).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780418246,"nonce":"sZnuU3sL5fVl42zWk3axJm7eg84=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEnQm9A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/205#issuecomment-4604569332"},"message":"Added the **segmentation timestamp fix** ([unh_marine_perception#28](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/28), PR #29) to Pre-flight. It corrects a constant ~123.5 ms stale-pose offset that made close buoys miss the costmap (the pose-timing half of the #26/#27 marking gap).\n\nKey point for whoever runs the validation: **the existing 2026-05-29 bag can't verify this fix** — the bug discarded the device timestamp, so the recorded segmentation stamps are baked wrong and the on-device node can't be bag-replayed. It needs **fresh data with the fixed build running**:\n- **Cheap gate (bench/dock, no water):** OAK powered + fixed build → `seg_stamp − ff_stamp ≈ 0` (was 123.5 ms). Do this before relying on the fix.\n- **On-water:** buoy marks in the costmap / horizon overlay aligns through the turn / δ-sweep ≈ 0.\n\nCode is reviewed (0 must-fix) and ready; empirical confirmation is the deployment's job.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1780419419,"nonce":"uuF5u9+iBRht/6gOh9hi3QfvCzE=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABEIINJ88AAAAGHISdZg"},"title":"Deployment 2026-06-02: UNH pier shakedown — survey lines + sensor/sonar readiness + OTH (pre-class)","was":"Deployment TBD: UNH pier shakedown — survey lines + sensor/sonar readiness + OTH (pre-class)"}]}